          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ट्रैफ़िक — ṭraifik — \"traffic\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शाम को सड़क पर बहुत ट्रैफ़िक होता है। śām ko saṛak par bahut ṭraifik hotā hai. There is a lot of traffic on the road in the evening."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ट्रैफ़िक (ṭraifik) is borrowed from English traffic, and like its source it takes no plural: बहुत ट्रैफ़िक, a lot of traffic."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
